<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2577>  Championess.
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2578>  III. xii. 43 to 45. On these stanzas see Introduction, p. xvi.
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2579>  IV. ii. 22 l. 7. aduizing] auising _1609_. For ‘aduize’ = observe cf.
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2580>  II. ix. 38 l. 3. Similarly we find ‘adward’ _1596_, but ‘award’ _1609_;
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2581>  conversely ‘dis-auentrous’ _1596_, ‘disaduentrous’ _1609_. Todd quotes
