<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2652>  for Granta, _i.e._ the Cam, as Upton noted.
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2653>  IV. xi. 52 l. 7. but] both _conj. edd._ The text is sound. Floods and
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2654>  fountains, though originally all derived from ocean, are yet akin to sky
<Spenser F.Q. 6.12.2655>  and sun.
